Testing [6. Face Attendance]: "how do I start face attendance?"
Reply: To begin a **face‑attendance (QR‑scan) session**, follow these steps based on your role:

---

### **If you’re a Faculty Member (generating the QR code)**  

1. **Open the Attendance page** in the admin portal.  
2. **Select “Live Dynamic QR Attendance Generator.”**  
3. **Choose the course** you want to record attendance for.  
4. **Set the session length** (e.g., 15 min, 30 min). The system will start a countdown.  
5. **Click “Generate QR.”**  
   - A dynamic QR code appears on your screen, refreshed automatically for the duration you set.  
   - Share your screen in the classroom or display the QR on a projector/monitor so students can see it.

6. **When the countdown ends**, the QR code expires automatically.  
7. **Review attendance** on the same page – students who scanned successfully will be marked **Present** (or **Late** if they scanned after the start time).  

---

### **If you’re a Student (scanning the QR code)**  

1. Go to the **Attendance page** (or the mobile app) and click **“Scan & Mark Attendance.”**  
2. Your device’s camera will activate – point it at the QR code displayed by the faculty.  
3. The system will read the code, verify the session, and automatically log you as **Present** (or **Late** if you’re after the start time).  
4. You’ll see a confirmation message on screen, and the attendance status will appear in your personal dashboard.  

> **Tip:** If the camera can’t read the QR, you can also manually enter the **session code** (shown beneath the QR) to mark your attendance.

---

### **Quick Checklist**

| Role | Action | What you’ll see |
|------|--------|-----------------|
| **Faculty** | Generate QR → Display → End countdown | Dynamic QR + timer |
| **Student** | Click “Scan & Mark Attendance” → Scan → Confirmation | Attendance marked (Present/Late) |

That’s it! Once the QR expires, any further scans are rejected, ensuring a clean, time‑bound attendance record. If you run into any issues (camera permissions, QR not scanning), double‑check that your device’s camera access is enabled and that the QR is fully visible on the screen.

